         "text": [
            {
               "text": "#### Conclusion\n\nIn this lesson, we learned that the origin of the numbers we use today is India and that there were different symbols for them.\n\nFurthermore, it is not only the people of India whom we give credit for these numbers. The Arabs, who chose, among the various representations of numbers, the one that was most useful to what they wanted, also deserve credit, which is why we call the numbers **Indo-Arabic**.\n\nHowever, we do not represent all numbers on our hands. And there are special reasons for this, which will be studied in the next lessons.",
               "source": [],
               "date_time": null,
